    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## NOT Operator\r\n\r\nThe NOT operator (`~`) reverses a Boolean condition. When it is combined with AND (`&`), each row must meet the first condition and must not meet the reversed condition.\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 1]\r\nRun the program. The current filter keeps superheroes whose `City` ends with `\"y\"` and whose `Alias` ends with `\"e\"`. Examine the results.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 2]\r\nModify the filter to keep superheroes whose `City` ends with `\"y\"` and whose `Alias` does **not** end with `\"e\"`.\r\n\r\nUse the NOT operator (`~`) and parentheses to reverse the Alias condition.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 3]\r\nRun the program and compare the results. Which superheroes were included or excluded after adding the NOT operator?\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [✅ Step 4]\r\nHow does the NOT condition work with the AND condition to determine which rows remain?\r\n:::",
